rs are limited (none in hand). Alternatively, you could aim for All Simples (no terminals/honors) or mixed hand. Given the exposed melds, W tiles are somewhat contested (across player has W4-W5-W6, previous has W6-W7-W8, next has W1-W2-W3). Discarding a W2 might be safest since you have three, and it reduces excess while keeping pairs (W4, T2). T2 is a safe discard with high unseen count. But keeping W2 triplet could lead to a pung, scoring points. However, with only 1 W2 left unseen, pung is unlikely unless drawn. Discarding T2 keeps the W2 triplet possibility and avoids breaking potential T chows (you have T5, T6, T7 which could form sequences).  \n\nBest choice: **Play T2** \u2013 It's a safe tile with many unseen, maintains your W2 triplet chance, and doesn't disrupt potential sequences in T or W suits.\n\nAnswer: Play T2"}
